    <briefdescription>
<para>This example demonstrates LMS and HSS signature verification using the hardened SHAKE block in the PMCL on Spartan UltraScale+. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><heading level="2">Procedure to link this example for DDR-less designs: </heading>
</para><para>PMC DMA reads the SHA source buffers below. Those buffers must reside in a memory region that both the PL and the PMC can access (PMCRAM). PMC DMA cannot complete a read from local BRAM, and the example then hangs in the DMA done wait.</para><para>SHARED_MEM is design dependent. Keep every byte of shared_mem inside the PMCRAM range assigned to the application. Stop before reserved PMCRAM such as the hooks table, hash block, and boot header.</para><para>PMC DMA reads these objects: SecureSha section .data.SecureSha 300 bytes PartialData inside SecureSha is the DMA buffer. LmsShake256Data section .data.LmsShake256Data 56 bytes HssShake256Data section .data.HssShake256Data 56 bytes DigestPrefixFields <ref refid="xsecure__lms__core_8c" kindref="compound">xsecure_lms_core.c</ref>, .bss 54 bytes LmsOtsSignVerifBuff <ref refid="xsecure__lms__core_8c" kindref="compound">xsecure_lms_core.c</ref>, .bss 4278 bytes TmpHashPerDigitBuff <ref refid="xsecure__lms__core_8c" kindref="compound">xsecure_lms_core.c</ref>, .bss 56 bytes LmsPubKeyTmpBuff <ref refid="xsecure__lms__core_8c" kindref="compound">xsecure_lms_core.c</ref>, .bss 86 bytes</para><para>The target(MB/MB-V) reads these objects. PMC DMA does not, so local memory is valid: LmsShake256Signature section .data.LmsShake256Signature 4460 bytes HssShake256Signature section .data.HssShake256Signature 4464 bytes LmsShake256PubKey (56 bytes) and HssShake256PubKey (60 bytes) AuthenticatedKey, DigestChecksum, TmpBuff, ExpectedPublicKey CurrentLmsQ and SignatureLengthConsumed, in .sbss XSECURE_D_MESG, XSECURE_D_PBLC, XSECURE_D_LEAF, XSECURE_D_INTR, in .rodata</para><para>The two signatures are about 9 KB. Leaving them in shared_mem pushes the library .bss out of a small PMCRAM window. Place those two sections in local memory, and place both .data and .bss in shared_mem. With the signatures in local memory, shared_mem must be at least 0x2000 bytes: the remaining .data is about 1.5 KB and .bss is about 5 KB.</para><para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Declare the region. ORIGIN is the PMCRAM base from the Vivado design.</para><para>shared_mem : ORIGIN = SHARED_MEM, LENGTH = 0x2000</para></listitem><listitem><para>Keep the signature sections in local memory. This output section must appear before the .data section, or *(.data.*) collects the signatures.</para><para>.lms_cpu_data : { *(.data.LmsShake256Signature) *(.data.HssShake256Signature) } &gt; local_bram_memory</para></listitem><listitem><para>Place .data and .bss in shared_mem:</para><para>.data : { . = ALIGN(64); __data_start = .; *(.data) *(.data.*) *(.gnu.linkonce.d.*) __data_end = .; } &gt; shared_mem</para><para>.bss (NOLOAD) : { . = ALIGN(16); __bss_start = .; *(.bss) *(.bss.*) *(.gnu.linkonce.b.*) *(COMMON) __bss_end = .; } &gt; shared_mem</para><para>ASSERT(__bss_end &lt;= ORIGIN(shared_mem) + LENGTH(shared_mem), &quot;LMS/HSS shared memory overflow&quot;)</para></listitem></orderedlist>
</para><para>MODIFICATION HISTORY: <preformatted>
